1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:07,700
The one percent Treaty is a piece of paper that says "stop spending so much on killing and spend a tiny bit on not dying."

2
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:16,400
More formally: every signatory nation redirects one percent of its annual military budget to the one percent Treaty Fund,

3
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:22,640
which finances global health initiatives like your decentralized institutes of health, or D.I.H.

4
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:29,760
It's legally binding, which means countries have to do it or feel mildly embarrassed at international conferences.

5
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:40,540
The Math. The Problem: The world spends two point seven two trillion dollars a year on military forces to maintain a delicate

6
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:49,540
balance of power. The Hack: If every nation reduces military spending by one percent *at the same time*, the balance of

7
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:54,060
power remains identical. No country becomes more vulnerable.

8
00:00:54,900 --> 00:01:04,780
The Prize: That one percent, a twenty-seven point two billion dollar a year river of cash, is redirected to cure all human

9
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:14,080
diseases. For comparison, twenty-seven point two billion dollars is about what Americans spend on Valentine's Day (flowers

10
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:20,720
and chocolate is more than curing cancer, apparently), and roughly what humans spend on pet food every three months.

11
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,760
Apparently too much to ask for curing diseases. How It Works.

12
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:33,800
Funding: Creates a twenty-seven point two billion dollar per year revenue stream for the one percent Treaty Fund.

13
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:43,420
Execution: A network of decentralized institutes of health, or D.I.H., subsidizes patient participation in a decentralized

14
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:54,080
framework for drug assessment (D.F.D.A. (a decentralized F.D.A.)), clinical trials that are forty-four point one times cheaper

15
00:01:54,080 --> 00:02:03,080
than the current model. Governance: Decentralized Autonomous Organization, or D.A.O., governed by smart contracts and global

16
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:10,699
population via Wishocracy. Transparency: All research, data, and spending published on public ledger.

17
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:19,100
This Isn't a Trade-Off. It's like if everyone in your neighborhood spent their life savings on attack dogs, and then called

18
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:23,520
it a "safe community" because all the dogs are equally vicious.

19
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:32,760
When every nation builds one percent fewer explosion devices *at the same time*, you get two good things: You become safer.

20
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:37,960
The global "you might all die by accident" temperature drops one percent.

21
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:43,800
Fewer chances of someone pressing the wrong button, which happens more than you'd think.

22
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:52,100
You stop dying from stupid things. That twenty-seven point two billion dollars pays sick people to try treatments instead

23
00:02:52,120 --> 00:03:00,180
of waiting for death. This is called a Pareto improvement, which is economist-speak for "everybody wins and nobody loses."

24
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:07,360
It's like finding out that eating less poison makes you both less poisoned AND wealthier because poison is expensive.

25
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:13,480
The Dead Capital Problem (Or: Why Bombs Are the Worst Investment Since Tulips).

26
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:20,740
Here's something nobody tells you: when countries "invest" in military hardware, they're not buying assets.

27
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:25,980
They're buying very expensive paperweights that occasionally explode.

28
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:33,860
A bridge. Generates economic activity daily (trucks move, people commute, value flows).

29
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:38,620
Lasts fifty to one hundred years. Makes everyone richer. Pretty to look at.

30
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:46,800
A missile. Sits in a hole doing nothing. Costs one point five million dollars a year just to keep it from rotting.

31
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:51,280
Can only destroy things (including itself). Makes everyone nervous.

32
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:58,780
This is what economists call "dead capital," resources trapped in a form that can't generate returns.

33
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:04,900
It's like if you converted your house into a pile of TNT. Sure, it's impressive.

34
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:13,240
But you can't live in it, rent it out, or do anything except eventually blow it up, at which point you have neither a house

35
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:22,780
nor TNT. As President Eisenhower (a five-star General who knew about killing professionally) put it: "Every gun that is

36
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:31,420
made, every warship launched, every rocket fired signifies, in the final sense, a theft from those who hunger and are not

37
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:39,860
fed, those who are cold and are not clothed." He literally ran the biggest military in history, and even HE thought you

38
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:48,380
were being ridiculous about this. A one percent treaty doesn't ask you to spend twenty-seven point two billion dollars curing

39
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:56,560
diseases. It asks you to stop wasting twenty-seven point two billion dollars on things that sit in holes making you poorer

40
00:04:56,560 --> 00:05:03,040
and less safe, and redirect those same papers to things that make you richer and less dead.

41
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:12,780
It's not spending. It's stopping wasting. The Reallocation: How to Redirect twenty-seven point two billion dollars a Year

42
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:21,180
(Legally). This is how you redirect twenty-seven point two billion dollars a year from the military budget to medicine.

43
